WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Secret of Whatsontap: Part 2</b>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:37.280
<b>The fateful day...</b>

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.450
Edwin-san said that they hadn't written 
down the nature of the offense yet.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.090
That is rather strange.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.450
Is it to prevent us from going into hiding?

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.300
That might be it.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.620
Do you think they're going to read the 
charges and arrest us right away?

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.300
According to Nikolaus-san,

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.410
if you get the death sentence 
for illegal trade of lager,

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.410
you get burned to a crisp!

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.170
The only thing I want crisped is bacon.

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.180
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:08.950
Quite admirable that you have not run away.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.950
<b>Damian (33) 
Backeshof's underling</b>

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:11.940
I'd rather not do this in front of the bar.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:15.950
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.550
Now, shall we begin?

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.060
<b>Backeshof (58) 
Chief of the City Council</b>

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.060
<b>Gernot (37)
 Tax Collector
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.950
Let's get this over with 
quickly, Gernot-kun.

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:29.170
I have a city council meeting at 
3 o'clock that I have to attend.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:30.620
I agree that we should settle this quickly.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.670
There will be many things that will 
need to be decided on at that meeting.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:37.080
That other meeting is also coming up soon.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:38.470
That other meeting?

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.920
The meeting with the neighboring countries.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.970
It's going to affect the reputation 
of the entire city if word

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.990
gets out that prohibited goods 
are being sold in Aitheria.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:50.990
It is my duty as a Backeshof to 
resolve this situation neatly.

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:53.020
Exactly as you say.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.050
It seems Gernot-san is on their side.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.200
Looks like it.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.190
I will now explain my investigation's 
methods and findings.

00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:06.020
I thought that if this place is 
indeed illegally selling lager,

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.770
by tracing where it originated, the 
full extent of the crime would

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.870
automatically become apparent.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.460
Right.

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.580
This is the information and 
investigation results that I received

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:17.710
from the imperial capital's Mikinokami.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:19.330
Mikinokami?

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.430
It's probably the controller 
of alcohol production.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:23.620
I see.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:27.180
By thoroughly investigating every employee 
associated with the Mikinokami,

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:31.140
it became apparent that significant amounts 
of lager were being illegally traded.

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.660
I knew it.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:38.030
Huh? It says that only 
37 barrels were leaked.

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:39.890
Is something wrong?

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:43.420
N-No, it just seems the number is quite low.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.160
Thirty-seven barrels of lager, something 
which must not be sold

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.750
under any circumstances, 
had been illegally sold.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.270
It is only appropriate to say 
that it is a significant amount.

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:52.460
Hm.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.350
How much is in a barrel?

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:58.420
I heard that it is about 250 glasses' worth.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:02.020
Which means, for Nobu, that's 
enough for about five days.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.310
That was my calculation as well.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:06.790
It's been half a year since 
this place has opened.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:11.560
If every barrel had come here, the 
calculation would fit exactly.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.670
I see, that's how it is.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.700
We're being made the scapegoat 
for this random crime...

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:25.010
Then all that remains is to arrest 
these two and to get a confession!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.410
That's not fair!

00:03:26.770 --> 00:03:30.030
Damian-kun, get someone 
from the palace guard.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.030
Right away!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.670
There is more to this story.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.130
Please take a look at this.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:38.100
What is this?

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:41.380
Actually, of the 37 barrels,

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:44.200
the whereabouts of 30 barrels are known.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:53.980
<b>United Kingdom          Ancient City         Empire         Monastery Territory

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.110
The regent of Oilia, our neighbor country,

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:49.370
has secretly bought them 
for a celebratory banquet.

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.080
An outrageous situation.

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.980
Then the other seven were probably sold here.

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.980
But then the calculations do not fit.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.300
If this place had been selling 
lager for half a year,

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.850
seven barrels would never cover it.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.400
I see, they mixed it!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.350
They mixed lager with ale!

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.960
That must be it!

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.600
But that is impossible as well.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.720
We already know that, of the remaining seven,

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:26.880
<b>United Kingdom          Ancient City         Empire         Monastery Territory

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:20.230
six barrels were transported 
to the southern region

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.720
of the empire and crossed the border there.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.460
That means there's one more barrel!

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.870
There is a barrel left over!

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.960
Yes. Just one single barrel.

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:32.020
Would the flavor of lager 
still be discernible

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:34.900
if you were to mix a single barrel with ale?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:40.020
Th-Then they're probably secretly 
producing lager right here!

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.340
A tiny place such as this 
creating lager, which

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.770
requires an extremely guarded 
production methodology?

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.750
Incidentally, Backeshof-san,

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:51.550
there is something I would like to ask you.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:53.780
Wh-What is it, Gernot-kun?

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.760
I have no patience for 
answering inane questions.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.280
It is a question of utmost importance.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.290
Why do you know what lager tastes like?

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.740
Could it be that Gernot-san is...

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.050
He's on our side.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:12.290
I, well, that is...

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:15.960
When I was still in the empire,
I was invited to a nobleman's banquet

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.290
and was allowed to sample it there.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.570
Which month of which year was 
this, and whose banquet was it?

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:25.560
Well, I, um... It, I mean...

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.900
Actually, the destination of the 
last barrel is known as well.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.690
It is here in Aitheria.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.190
Oh, then everything is settled!

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:37.220
As I thought, that last barrel 
came here, to this place!

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.710
Backeshof-san,

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:42.950
the last barrel was purchased by 
the Backeshof trading company.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.820
The only thing I did not know 
yet was who drank it!

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.220
Damian?!

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:50.800
He ran away.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:51.440
Yeah.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.100
It is fine.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.330
Ow, ow...

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:58.470
Nikolaus-san and Hans-san!

00:05:58.470 --> 00:05:59.740
And Berthold-san as well!

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.010
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:08.280
<b>Hans (23)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:08.280
<b>Nikolaus (24)
Palace Guard
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.470
Gernot-san asked us to be here.

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.270
He told us to arrest this guy 
if he made a run for it.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:09.860
Exactly.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:13.950
I called them here to arrest the 
criminals behind the illegal trade.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:16.460
Arrest that man as well!

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.580
Gernot, you bastard!

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:25.100
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company Commander of 
Aitheria Palace Guards aka "the Devil"</b>

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:21.150
Backeshof!

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:25.100
Don't think you can get away with your 
crime of trading prohibited goods!

00:06:31.880 --> 00:06:35.540
It looks like Gernot-san had 
everything figured out.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.450
It's going to be a busy day.

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:42.220
There are so many things that need 
to be decided at the meeting.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:46.670
Including the successor of Backeshof.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:50.730
Prosit!

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:56.410
But Gernot really is something.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.240
He was like a hunting dog that had 
been unleashed on a deeg beast.

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:01.630
Speaking of, where is tonight's star?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.060
He declined the invitation, saying 
he had too much work to do.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.820
He doesn't like these sorts of 
gatherings. He's a cool person.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:11.380
<b>Lorenz (50)
Glass Craft Guild Meister</b>

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.760
I wonder if he did all of this because 
of his passion for the eel bentos.

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:14.350
<b>Holger (50) 
Blacksmith Guild Meister. 
Member of the city council.</b>

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:13.080
Actually, that's not it.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.920
It wasn't eel, but a dish called napolitan.

00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:18.070
Napolitan?

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:21.530
We've never served Napolitan at our place.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.350
Do you know anything about 
that, Shinobu-chan?

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.860
Huh?! No I don't know
anything about napolitan.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:31.100
I guess everything you did 
was in vain, huh, Hans?

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.360
Do not say it, you idiot!

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:36.450
He was collecting signatures 
to reduce Nobu's sentence.

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:38.060
I believe it was 118 signatures?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.870
It was 123!

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:41.510
And look who's talking.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:42.920
Hey, wait, nobody needs to know that.

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.760
He went as far as to fall to his knees in 
front of his ex-ex-girlfriend's from the

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:49.370
drink wholesale business and the 
ex-girlfriend whose widowed mother has

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:52.480
a brewing business, trying to get a 
counterfeit contract for trading ale!

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.360
Stop it! Those things are cooler 
when they're not talked about!

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:59.750
Hans-kun, your father was 
quite something, too.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:00.890
Holger!

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.410
He was going around,

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.680
canvassing the city council members 
who are on Backeshof's side,

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.130
trying to sway them to not ruin this place!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.280
You also threatened the 
Backeshof Trading Company

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:10.130
saying you'd stop dealing with them!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.190
That's because they're cretins who push their

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:13.760
unreasonable demands with everything!

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.500
Lorenz-san, Holger-san, please calm down.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.760
Oh yeah, the three guys from the 
water transport guilds were also

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:26.060
preparing funds in case this 
place was about to be bought out.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.420
Our deacon here also asked 
the church for help, right?

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:33.420
<b>Edwin (70)
Deacon of the 
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:33.420
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.190
Everybody was doing everything 
they can to help this place.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:37.430
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:40.910
I'm sorry that I couldn't be of any help.

00:08:40.730 --> 00:08:44.170
<b>Hermina (16)
Waitress at Nobu. Berthold's wife</b>

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:45.510
Everybody knows that you 
were praying every day.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:46.400
Right!

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:50.420
All right. The katsu skewers are done!

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:53.560
Katsu skewers! That's like fritters, right?

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:54.450
<b>Katsu Skewer Medley</b>

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:54.450
<b>Fried to crispy perfection, you'll end up 
eating a lot since there's so many different types</b>

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.690
Looks like these have a slightly different 
tastiness to them than tempura.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:08:59.350
Please dip them in this sauce before eating.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.570
Oh, but double-dipping is forbidden.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:04.470
All right, then. I'll start with this Spargel.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:05.260
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:07.460
Oh!

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:10.960
There's meat wrapped around the Spargel!

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:13.450
It goes really well with 
the umami of the meat!

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.880
I've got kisu and crab!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:22.220
The contrast of the crunchy outside 
with the fluffy inside is perfect!

00:09:22.220 --> 00:09:24.370
It's falling apart in my mouth!

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.250
Let's see how the shrimp is.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:27.280
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:29.350 --> 00:09:32.960
The springy texture of the shrimp and 
the crispy breading are so good!

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:34.380
And to go with that...

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.390
<b>Fizz</b>

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.280
Nothing better than a whatsontap.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:40.730
<b>Crunch</b>

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.080
This lotus root's substantial 
texture really goes perfectly

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.830
with the breading's crispy texture.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:49.530
These have the same shape, but 
their sizes are different.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:50.390
What are they?

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.310
The small ones are ginnan, 
the big ones are quail eggs.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.380
Today I'm going to use all the 
ingredients I have in the pantry.

00:09:57.890 --> 00:10:00.370
Are you going to be okay for tomorrow?!

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:04.020
Well, if we run out of stuff, we'll just have to close for a while.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:07.310
What?! That would be a big blow when 
the place just got off the hook!

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:10.550
Right?

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.680
Hey, Taishou.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.850
What is it, Shinobu-chan?

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:20.190
It's really lucky that we were able 
to open up shop in this town.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.560
Yeah.

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:22.640
This is amazing!

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.270
Hey, that was mine!

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we have Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:44.030
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:42.330
You can make very tasty katsu skewers 
with just a single frying pan!

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:49.720
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:51.040
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:51.070 --> 00:10:54.920
It really is good to have 
Gernot-san as an ally, huh?

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:56.750
<b>Ryuuta Kijima</b>

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:56.750
<b>Grew up in a household where both his grandmother and his mother were culinary researchers,
so he got into cooking at an early age. Now he's a culinary researcher who's popular
for his simple but serious recipes and his fun presentation.</b>

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.260
He'd be really scary to 
have as an enemy, though.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:56.760
So true!

00:10:56.760 --> 00:10:59.120
Katsu skewers really get 
the party going, huh?

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.770
I always love eating 
those in a restaurant.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:01.790
Me, too. I love them!

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.560
But making those at home 
really is a hassle.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.690
Yeah, it really is a lot of work.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:08.520
I'd like to try to make some katsu 
skewers you don't have to fry.

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:09.120
<b>Katsu skewer style 
 without using oil to fry</b>

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:10.010
Is that even possible?

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:14.150
<b>Grilled shrimp and vegetables - katsu skewer style 

00:11:10.010 --> 00:11:11.940
Shrimp, vegetables, panko, and oil?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.150
That's just regular katsu skewer stuff!

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.120
We're going to just cut off the 
hard part of the asparagus.

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:29.580
<b>Grilled shrimp & vegetables 
Katsu skewer style</b>

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.240
The skin on the bottom is rather tough, 
so we'll use the peeler for that.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:20.980
Roger.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:23.320
And then?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.110
Cut them so they're about 4 fingers wide.

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:25.870
Got it!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:29.590
I like cutting the pepper so 
that they can easily be eaten.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:33.300
So that even girls
can eat it in one bite!

00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:36.030
Slice open the back of the shrimp like this.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:36.610
Right, right.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.800
Begin by skewering the vegetables.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:41.110
Ah, just like that.

00:11:41.110 --> 00:11:41.750
What's next?

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.720
Next up is the asparagus.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:44.400
Good.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:47.840
And the shrimp last.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:48.840
Why is the order like this?

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.930
When you grill shrimp, it gets tighter,

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.580
which makes it harder to get off the skewer.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:53.460
Oh, right.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:58.500
<b>By using the shrimp last,
the skewer doesn't fall apart</b>

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:57.100
So to prevent the skewer from falling 
apart, putting the shrimp last is good.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.520
And the breading?

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.400
I'd like to try making crispy panko,

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.050
and then sprinkle that on 
top of the grilled skewer,

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:04.080
making it katsu skewer style.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:04.430
Oh!

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.660
Adding the panko.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.400
A tablespoon of vegetable oil.

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.650
Pan fry the panko until it gets crispy.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:12.870
What should it look like?

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.950
Keep frying until it has the 
color of tonkatsu breading.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:17.650
<b>The panko should be fried without letting it burn,
until it has the color of tonkatsu breading</b>

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.480
Careful so it doesn't burn!

00:12:18.480 --> 00:12:21.800
It has a nice color now, 
so I'll turn off the heat.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:22.720
That's the color!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:24.820
Now let's season the skewers.

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:27.160
Sprinkle salt and pepper on both sides.

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:29.020
Then place them in the pan.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.090
Don't forget to lightly 
coat the pan with oil.

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:36.200
It takes about two minutes like this 
for the surface to get browned.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.910
Let's see how this one is doing.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:39.670
Oh, it's looking good.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.140
Oh yes, that's so seductive!

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.350
Like this, cooking it through 
will be a bit difficult,

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:51.050
so we're going to cover it and steam 
grill it for about 2 minutes.

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:53.670
Two minutes are up, so let's take off the lid.

00:12:53.670 --> 00:12:57.620
Wow, both the aroma and 
the look are perfect!

00:12:57.620 --> 00:12:59.150
Now we can take them out.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:01.460
Oh, so grilled skewers, just like that.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:05.840
And now we're going to cover these with 
the panko that we pan fried before.

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.680
Oh, that's some really 
fragrant katsu skewers!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:13.290
This way, you can make skewers 
with your favorite ingredients

00:13:10.030 --> 00:13:18.880
<b>Grilled shrimp and vegetables 
Katsu skewer style</b>

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.810
and cover them with crispy panko.

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:16.780
Using this method, you can make these

00:13:16.780 --> 00:13:18.900
without all the fuss, so please do try it.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.560
I promise you that it'll make 
the whatsontap even tastier.

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:24.210
Make grilled skewers, then 
toss crispy panko on top!

00:13:22.050 --> 00:13:33.020
<b>Today's high-speed footage</b>

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:26.800
It really does taste like katsu skewers!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:28.920
It's so easy, it's so fancy!

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:32.080
Everybody, do try making 
a katsu skewer party!

